6327 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The issue arises when one of the reserved writers is blocklisted by the Strike token\056 For example\054 if USDC is used as the Strike asset and a reserved writer is blacklisted by USDC\054 the Strike transfer from the buyer to that writer will revert\056\nSince the entire exercise process is atomic\054 this revert causes the whole exercise\050\051 transaction to fail\056 Moreover\054 the buyer cannot choose which writer to exercise against\054 as the function always processes writers according to the reservedWritersByBuyer array\056\nAs a result\054 a single blocklisted writer can prevent the buyer from exercising their option altogether\056 The buyer may therefore be unable to receive the expected payout despite having purchased the option and paid the premium\056\nNote that the issue is broader when the Strike token is an ERC777\056 An attacker can leverage the ERC777 callback mechanism to block the exercise process in a similar manner to the blocklist issue described above\056\nFurthermore\054 if the Base token is an ERC777\054 a malicious writer can also DoS the option purchase process\056 By placing a position at the smallest price lot\054 the writer can use the ERC777 callback to revert the token transfer when a buyer attempts to purchase the option\054 causing the entire purchase transaction to fail\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 6328 0 R
     /Pg 3022 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

